<title>Why render on the server?</title>

<nav><a href="/">Home</a> <a href="/article">Article</a> <a href="/account">Account</a></nav>
<article>
  <h1>Why render on the server?</h1>
  <p>A visitor should be able to read a page before any script runs. This article was rendered by the Rust renderer during the build and is served as a static file.</p>
  <p>It has no event handlers and no state, so the compiler emitted no JavaScript for it at all.</p>
</article>

